# Normalise line endings on every checkout, whatever the platform or a contributor's core.autocrlf
# setting, so the tree is consistent across the matrix. C# 11 raw string literals normalise every
# source line break to \n regardless of the file's line endings, so this pinning is about a uniform
# tree, not about protecting test expectations from a CRLF checkout. `text=auto` marks the remaining
# text files text; the explicit `eol=lf` entries pin the build- and test-relevant ones.
* text=auto
*.cs text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.sln text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.targets text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.editorconfig text eol=lf
*.gitignore text eol=lf